  "TITLE": "Homeostasis:<br>Correction by Opposition",
  "LEAD": "Cells and bodies stay stable by letting every deviation trigger a response that pushes the other way: too much glucose releases insulin, too little releases glucagon. This negative feedback loop turns a fragile set point into a self-repairing one. A central bank does the same with interest rates, raising them when inflation overshoots and cutting them when it sags, so that no one has to predict the next shock.",
